+
+### SVG escaping
+
+A chart draws text that does not come from the code: `--label` texts, `--builds` ids, plugin names from `plugins.jsonl`, step
+names from `pauses.jsonl`, and the versions in `environment.txt`. `report.py` therefore escapes each value once, where it is
+written into the markup (`esc`), and never when it is read: a label such as `</text><script>alert(1)</script>` stays text
+inside its element, and a quote in `--label` cannot close the `aria-label` attribute and add one of its own. Characters XML 1.0
+forbids - the C0 controls other than tab, line feed and carriage return, a lone surrogate, U+FFFE and U+FFFF - become U+FFFD, so
+a document parses whatever the results folder holds; every other character, Unicode included, is written as it is. Escaping
+before `text_width` would measure `&amp;` as five characters and move the bars, so the layout is untouched: an existing results
+folder produces the charts it produced before, byte for byte.
+
+The Markdown tables `report.py` prints are not escaped: a label holding `|` or a line break still breaks a table cell.
+
+```
+python3 bench/test_report_svg.py
+```
+
+The tests use the standard library only: the escape rule itself, adversarial labels and metadata through `report.py`'s own
+command line, ordinary labels unchanged, and every generated chart parsed with `xml.etree.ElementTree`.
